  "title": "Carving of the Tripitaka Koreana",
  "summary": "Goryeo Korea carved the Tripitaka Koreana, a collection of Buddhist scriptures, between 1236 and 1251, ordering a new set during the Mongol invasions after the first was destroyed. It filled 81,258 wooden printing blocks, which were moved to Haeinsa temple in 1398 and are still kept there. UNESCO lists the blocks in its Memory of the World register.",
